hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2741","Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari narrated to us: Ibn Bakr informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us. (Another chain:) And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr and al-Walid ibn 'Ata', from al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Rabi'ah, who said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd said: Al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah came as a delegate to 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan during his caliphate, and 'Abd al-Malik said: ""I do not think that Abu Khubayb"" - meaning Ibn al-Zubayr - ""heard from 'Aishah what he claimed to have heard from her."" Al-Harith said: ""Indeed, I heard it from her myself."" He said: ""What did you hear her say?"" He said: She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Your people fell short in the construction of the House (the Ka'bah), and were it not for the recency of their covenant with disbelief, I would have restored what they left out of it. So if it occurs to your people after me to rebuild it, then come"
